<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trento</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Trent, Tridentum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trento is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adige">Adige</a> river in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and the capital of the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trentino">Trentino</a>. It began as the Roman town of Tridentum, became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> duchy and from 1027 was ruled by prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-trent">Council of Trent</a> met there between 1545 and 1563. Austrian from 1803, it passed to Italy after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trento.jpg" alt="Trento" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BelPatty86 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trento_visione_d%27insieme_6.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
